1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:05,550
The girl from Roopkund is alive.

2
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:13,240
Kyoichi Nanase claimed she was dead.

3
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:15,450
Shiharu is dead.

4
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:19,230
<i>But I don't believe him.</i>

5
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:21,480
You won't look into anything unnecessary?

6
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:24,720
<i>If anything, he seems desperate to hide her.</i>

7
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:29,060
I want nothing to do with this.

8
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:32,070
Please, wait. Shii...

9
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:35,850
The girl from Roopkund needs you!

10
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:39,640
She was already weak the last time I saw her.

11
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:44,880
You're the only person who can save her!

12
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:10,960
<i>Shiharu was an artificially made human being.</i>

13
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,210
Haruka.

14
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:50,870
- What are you doing?
- Don't you love me?

15
00:01:50,870 --> 00:01:52,810
You're acting strange.

16
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:54,990
What do you love about me?

17
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:56,190
Huh?

18
00:01:56,190 --> 00:01:58,620
Answer me.

19
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:00,030
I love everything about you.

20
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:01,690
And what's "everything"?

21
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:07,700
Your pretty hair, your beauty,
your intelligence - everything.

22
00:02:08,490 --> 00:02:14,210
Then you wouldn't love me
if I became bald, ugly, and dumb.

23
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:20,250
Well, that wouldn't be you anymore, would it?

24
00:02:23,490 --> 00:02:25,080
Yeah.

25
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,940
I think so, too.

26
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,510
Shiharu?

27
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:33,050
Wait.

28
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,230
Shiharu.

29
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:38,750
Shiharu!

30
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:41,270
If something's bothering you, tell me.

31
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:42,210
I already did!

32
00:02:42,210 --> 00:02:43,530
I don't understand.

33
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:44,900
That's fine.

34
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,380
Don't make things more confusing for me.

35
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:52,080
I don't want you to understand.

36
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,970
Does that clear things up?

37
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,180
Fine.

38
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:40,850
[The mystery of his sister's life and death]
[Despair hidden within the truth]

39
00:03:40,850 --> 00:03:42,760
I'm home.

40
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:51,200
[log.7]

41
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:52,960
Shiharu?

42
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:02,680
Shiharu?

43
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,100
Aren't you home?

44
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:13,630
Shiharu?

45
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:26,040
So it's been quite some time
since she's lost her ability to walk.

46
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:31,240
Could you tell me more
about the marks on her skin?

47
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:36,790
The ones I saw were on her hands and neck.

48
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,820
I see.

49
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:44,190
The clone's DNA suffered damages after all.

50
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:51,190
But if you're telling the truth,

51
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:55,630
then it's entirely possible
she's still alive.

52
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,450
Though I suspect she doesn't have long.

53
00:05:01,450 --> 00:05:07,640
Nanase and Ishimizaki did well
to keep her thriving without me.

54
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:10,830
Dr. Senba.

55
00:05:10,830 --> 00:05:14,320
Please ask Mr. Nanase where he's keeping her.

56
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:17,540
- Me?
- I know he would tell you.

57
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:20,950
Because you can save her.

58
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:23,500
He would never pass up such an opportunity.

59
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:27,640
My answer is "no".

60
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:32,660
I can't afford to get involved anymore.

61
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:36,020
You aren't worried about her?

62
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:39,750
I am interested. But that's all.

63
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:42,520
You brought her into this world.

64
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:46,590
Your trivial moral reasoning
won't change my mind.

65
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:53,100
So you don't think of her as your daughter?

66
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,220
My "daughter".

67
00:05:57,750 --> 00:06:02,170
A child I knew nothing about for 30 years,
my "daughter".

68
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:06,520
They ought to realize their selfish desires

69
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:13,020
ruined any potential
for scientific advancements.

70
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:16,220
Nanase is especially guilty in that regard.

71
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:19,000
- I just...
- Quiet.

72
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,510
Their actions have brought
very real consequences to my life.

73
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:25,940
I just want her be alive.

74
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:30,310
I called my security on you.

75
00:06:30,310 --> 00:06:33,170
Feel free to stay if you want to be arrested.

76
00:06:33,170 --> 00:06:38,010
I can't be entertaining this any longer.

77
00:06:55,190 --> 00:06:57,070
What are you doing here?

78
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:59,110
Sir.

79
00:06:59,110 --> 00:07:02,150
Isn't there something
you've been hiding from me?

80
00:07:03,110 --> 00:07:04,950
What are you referring to?

81
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:09,040
As I was looking into our finances,

82
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:15,180
I noticed some funds related to "log.0"
were still being utilized.

83
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:20,410
They were deftly hidden
through distributions to a shell corporation.

84
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:27,200
Sir, did you think I wouldn't notice?

85
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:31,530
You taught me to be thorough.

86
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:33,800
What is the money being used for?

87
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:37,890
Order me to keep it under wraps, and I will.

88
00:07:37,890 --> 00:07:40,480
But must I be kept in the dark as well?

89
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:46,700
Please, tell me the truth.

90
00:07:47,730 --> 00:07:50,230
Is "log.0" still active?

91
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:56,810
I wouldn't know.

92
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:24,050
Morning. Did you get it?

93
00:08:24,050 --> 00:08:27,120
Yes. Everything pertaining to Roopkund.

94
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:29,130
Score.

95
00:08:29,130 --> 00:08:31,630
Want a drink to celebrate?

96
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:35,200
Maybe it's too early for that.

97
00:08:38,350 --> 00:08:41,660
Take a seat wherever.

98
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:44,030
I run this bar.

99
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:45,780
Just kidding.

100
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:50,410
I rented the place so we'd get some privacy.

101
00:08:50,410 --> 00:08:56,230
Honestly, I drank till morning
'cause I didn't want to go home.

102
00:09:00,230 --> 00:09:06,420
Was too scared to find myself alone and all.

103
00:09:07,870 --> 00:09:14,000
Some crazy truth we got ourselves, huh?

104
00:09:16,410 --> 00:09:20,530
Do you believe them?
It sounds ridiculous to me.

105
00:09:20,530 --> 00:09:28,100
I'm more convinced,
knowing Kayoko Senba is involved.

106
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,410
Excuse me.

107
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:32,870
- Sir.
- Yes?

108
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:34,960
You won't release our names, right?

109
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:38,980
No, of course not. I promise.

110
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:45,900
I only ask because of the rumors.
Not like I believe them, but...

111
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:47,370
Rumors?

112
00:09:48,050 --> 00:09:51,480
They say those who bring trouble to Plantae

113
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:55,550
are punished by the spirit of the Holy One.

114
00:09:58,770 --> 00:10:01,770
I assume my fellow journalist, Onodera,

115
00:10:01,770 --> 00:10:07,170
was murdered by this "spirit" of theirs.

116
00:10:08,230 --> 00:10:10,660
All that's left is his bones,
and nothing else.

117
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:26,720
<i>That man, Ushio.</i>

118
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:31,080
Is he acting on Plantae's orders?

119
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:33,340
Who else would boss him around?

120
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:37,050
Kyoichi Nanase.

121
00:10:38,230 --> 00:10:42,070
Their interests do align.

122
00:10:42,070 --> 00:10:46,000
But I'm more inclined to believe
this is all Plantae.

123
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:52,470
The biggest surprise here,

124
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:57,460
is that they went and created a person.

125
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:01,150
No country in the world
would legalize human clones.

126
00:11:01,150 --> 00:11:04,190
But the technology in creating one
holds great value.

127
00:11:04,190 --> 00:11:06,750
Medical advancements would surge forth.

128
00:11:10,230 --> 00:11:12,580
Find evidence of this clone at once.

129
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:15,200
We'll contact the main branch
in China afterwards.

130
00:11:16,650 --> 00:11:18,100
Yes, sir.

131
00:11:25,690 --> 00:11:28,410
I've checked its contents.

132
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:32,790
Everything pertains to the making of a clone.

133
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:40,210
So it's all true.

134
00:11:40,210 --> 00:11:44,650
There really was an artificial human

135
00:11:44,650 --> 00:11:48,290
walking among us.

136
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:53,000
Sends shivers down my spine, I tell you.

137
00:11:54,620 --> 00:12:00,950
I bet Onodera felt the same way.

138
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:07,570
We can't help it.

139
00:12:07,570 --> 00:12:10,040
It's what makes us journalists.

140
00:12:11,450 --> 00:12:15,390
I'll be sure his findings
see a proper conclusion.

141
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:20,050
I don't want you to write about this.

142
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:23,460
My sister's existence will be
known to the world.

143
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,400
Don't worry.

144
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:32,460
I won't be hasty
about publishing our evidence.

145
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:36,060
I'll hold onto the data.

146
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:38,670
It'll be useful
as a bargaining chip to find my sister.

147
00:12:38,670 --> 00:12:41,330
I promise not to put you in a bind.

148
00:12:41,330 --> 00:12:44,210
Publishing an article will do that anyway.

149
00:12:44,210 --> 00:12:47,560
Numerous people have died over this.

150
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:51,200
Leave it be, and more will follow.

151
00:12:52,690 --> 00:12:55,190
You plan to publish the article immediately.

152
00:12:57,030 --> 00:13:02,150
These people are killing folks left and right

153
00:13:02,150 --> 00:13:05,810
all to keep this girl under wraps.

154
00:13:05,810 --> 00:13:07,200
The public deserves to know.

155
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,580
Then what happens to my sister?

156
00:13:12,850 --> 00:13:15,140
"Punished by the spirit of the Holy One".

157
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,840
Hear what I'm getting at?

158
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:22,740
What do you mean?

159
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:25,180
The "Holy One" they're so scared of,

160
00:13:26,150 --> 00:13:30,390
is your sister, the Holy Woman.

161
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:34,790
What sort of assumption is that?

162
00:13:34,790 --> 00:13:37,020
I won't beat around the bush.

163
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:42,100
I suspect your younger sister
is the one behind all this.

164
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:46,160
What?

165
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:48,480
Why Shiharu?

166
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:52,020
She wants to protect herself.

167
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:54,790
Your sister is the Holy Woman.

168
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:58,390
If anyone could control Ushio, it'd be her.

169
00:13:58,930 --> 00:14:03,020
And your father.

170
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:06,240
He was all in on helping Plantae

171
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:09,220
create a clone.

172
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:14,010
It wouldn't surprise me
if he obeys the Holy Woman, too.

173
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:17,570
- Give me that!
- Hey!

174
00:14:17,570 --> 00:14:19,380
Think about it!

175
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,750
Shiharu Nanase is an artificial human being!

176
00:14:21,750 --> 00:14:25,040
Can you really call
a thing like her your sister?

177
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,890
Let go!

178
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,050
[Yui Ishimizaki]

179
00:14:40,110 --> 00:14:41,730
[Yui Ishimizaki]

180
00:14:41,730 --> 00:14:45,660
[Kyoichi told me everything about Shiharu]

181
00:14:49,990 --> 00:14:52,510
[Senba]

182
00:14:53,670 --> 00:14:56,550
Damn it, why isn't anyone answering?

183
00:14:56,550 --> 00:15:00,700
Tomoe is a stay-at-home mother.
I assumed she would be around.

184
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:02,750
Guess we'll wait.

185
00:15:02,750 --> 00:15:06,330
We can't stay long.
We're ignoring orders to be here.

186
00:15:06,330 --> 00:15:10,720
Still a bootlicker for headquarters?

187
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:13,950
Tada.

188
00:15:13,950 --> 00:15:15,810
Damn it!

189
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:47,090
I thought you'd feel more comfortable
meeting where there's a crowd.

190
00:15:49,050 --> 00:15:52,580
- Want a croquette?
- What did he tell you about Shiharu?

191
00:15:57,370 --> 00:15:59,080
Everything.

192
00:16:00,190 --> 00:16:04,880
Roopkund, the process... Everything.

193
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:07,120
Where is Shiharu?

194
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:13,600
Kyoichi said she had passed away.

195
00:16:14,330 --> 00:16:17,120
- But I think she's alive!
- Who are you?

196
00:16:20,650 --> 00:16:22,470
Answer me.

197
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:32,550
I'm Ishimizaki's daughter, Mari.

198
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,150
What?

199
00:16:37,150 --> 00:16:40,840
I met Mari. She was in a wheelchair.

200
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,130
The Professor called that girl his daughter.

201
00:16:43,130 --> 00:16:47,190
My father lied to you.

202
00:16:47,190 --> 00:16:49,000
He had no choice.

203
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,870
Why?

204
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:53,620
Why did he have to lie?

205
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:03,020
Who were you looking for all this time?

206
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:27,430
The Professor brought that girl in,
on the day of a heavy storm?

207
00:17:28,210 --> 00:17:31,550
Right.

208
00:17:32,910 --> 00:17:35,860
But you can't tell me who this girl is.

209
00:17:41,330 --> 00:17:42,830
Why?

210
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:49,020
Because I promised her I wouldn't.

211
00:17:49,990 --> 00:17:52,060
What's the point of a promise like that?

212
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:20,550
I'm not hiding anything else from you.

213
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:26,190
I know I'm asking the impossible,
but I want you to trust me.

214
00:18:26,190 --> 00:18:30,220
Haruka, I promise you and I share a goal.

215
00:18:37,310 --> 00:18:38,850
Alright.

216
00:18:47,570 --> 00:18:52,170
I'm sorry about your father.
That must have been difficult.

217
00:18:56,940 --> 00:19:02,060
He was one of the few individuals
who truly understood me.

218
00:19:06,330 --> 00:19:12,810
He'd always entertain my thoughts, too.

219
00:19:12,810 --> 00:19:15,550
I could tell him anything.

220
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:22,680
But in these last few years, he changed.

221
00:19:28,310 --> 00:19:32,800
<i>The last time I saw him</i>

222
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:40,620
<i>was another day I couldn't ask
about his secrets.</i>

223
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:48,970
Didn't notice you there.

224
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:52,090
How's Shii?

225
00:19:52,090 --> 00:19:54,530
She's sleeping right now.

226
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:56,410
Let her rest.

227
00:19:57,270 --> 00:19:59,520
Shiharu is okay.

228
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:01,590
I promise.

229
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,410
Okay.

230
00:20:11,270 --> 00:20:15,220
Dad. Have you been eating?

231
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:18,430
Huh?

232
00:20:19,250 --> 00:20:21,540
Oh, yes. I have.

233
00:20:23,510 --> 00:20:25,730
Let me whip up something for you.

234
00:20:29,450 --> 00:20:31,890
What?

235
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:36,010
Mari...

236
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:38,830
I don't need to worry about you anymore.

237
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:47,150
Everyone will come to love
your endearing attitude.

238
00:20:48,770 --> 00:20:51,200
Stop it, you're embarrassing me.

239
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:55,450
Never change, Mari.

240
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:59,210
I won't.

241
00:20:59,210 --> 00:21:05,400
My father was prepared
to confess about Roopkund.

242
00:21:07,030 --> 00:21:09,090
I regret not asking.

243
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:14,790
I should have pestered him more.

244
00:21:15,570 --> 00:21:18,750
Maybe something would have changed.

245
00:21:20,590 --> 00:21:25,470
That regret is why I'm so determined now.

246
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:33,020
It'll be okay, Haruka.

247
00:21:34,230 --> 00:21:40,080
We will find Shiharu. I promise.

248
00:21:49,150 --> 00:21:52,170
What if...

249
00:21:54,690 --> 00:21:58,370
What if we find Shiharu, and she's changed?

250
00:21:59,780 --> 00:22:01,830
What do you mean?

251
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:08,620
Someone suspects Shiharu
is the one behind all these incidents.

252
00:22:09,210 --> 00:22:11,400
That's impossible.

253
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:13,420
It's really not.

254
00:22:13,420 --> 00:22:19,040
Anyone who suspects her is a fool.

255
00:22:22,190 --> 00:22:23,710
Yeah.

256
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:28,140
They're a fool.

257
00:22:31,790 --> 00:22:33,090
I don't understand.

258
00:22:33,090 --> 00:22:37,690
Like I said, I didn't get the evidence.

259
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:40,780
I'll try again from another angle.

260
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:45,150
Kayoko Senba seems like my best bet.

261
00:22:45,150 --> 00:22:47,770
What happened to Haruka Nanase?

262
00:22:47,770 --> 00:22:49,600
He gave me nothing to work with.

263
00:22:50,690 --> 00:22:52,610
I'll change his mind.

264
00:22:52,610 --> 00:22:54,860
Tell me how to reach him.

265
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:58,200
That's not my information to give.

266
00:22:58,200 --> 00:23:01,490
- I know it's written in there.
- Hey, no touching.

267
00:23:01,490 --> 00:23:03,950
This is a journalist's soul.

268
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:10,180
Kayoko Senba, you said?

269
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:14,580
That's right. Let's forget Haruka Nanase.

270
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:22,280
I'm so sorry.

271
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:24,230
I only have instant foods.

272
00:23:24,230 --> 00:23:28,620
But you should definitely eat something.

273
00:23:30,410 --> 00:23:32,390
I'll heat up the croquettes.

274
00:23:34,930 --> 00:23:37,360
Right, I should boil the water first.

275
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:40,470
Here, I'll do it.

276
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:43,640
Thank you.

277
00:23:55,410 --> 00:23:57,020
Haruka.

278
00:23:58,110 --> 00:24:02,510
Could you tell me more about Shiharu?

279
00:24:02,510 --> 00:24:04,250
Huh?

280
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:06,830
You told me stories about her before.

281
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:11,120
Please?

282
00:24:18,150 --> 00:24:20,720
She once said she wanted a part-time job.

283
00:24:22,740 --> 00:24:28,560
<i>What I considered a pain,
was a source of wonder to her.</i>

284
00:24:29,350 --> 00:24:31,580
What're you doing?

285
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:33,200
Welcome home.

286
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:35,380
I just finished reading.

287
00:24:35,380 --> 00:24:37,180
Then let's go to the gallery.

288
00:24:37,910 --> 00:24:40,520
Haruka, you don't work part-time?

289
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,290
No, why?

290
00:24:42,290 --> 00:24:44,080
It seems fun.

291
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:49,110
"Manager, that's not what the manual says."

292
00:24:49,110 --> 00:24:50,820
Huh? What manager?

293
00:24:50,820 --> 00:24:53,370
I just wanted to try saying it.

294
00:24:53,370 --> 00:24:56,910
"That's not my mistake."

295
00:24:56,910 --> 00:25:00,270
"I meant to come in, really."

296
00:25:00,270 --> 00:25:02,000
Is that for when you skip work?

297
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,620
I don't know.

298
00:25:04,510 --> 00:25:08,630
I wouldn't know.

299
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:17,390
Work is more trouble than it's worth.

300
00:25:18,620 --> 00:25:23,900
Then how's this?
"Hasegawa, we share a shift on Christmas."

301
00:25:23,900 --> 00:25:25,850
Who the heck is Hasegawa?

302
00:25:25,850 --> 00:25:28,520
"No venting allowed, Haruka."

303
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:30,380
I'm employed with you?

304
00:25:35,210 --> 00:25:38,250
I usually started our conversations.

305
00:25:38,250 --> 00:25:42,840
Shiharu would be too absorbed in a book.

306
00:25:58,630 --> 00:26:01,020
Thank you.

307
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:04,060
For telling me about her.

308
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:02,510
It's no use.

309
00:27:02,510 --> 00:27:05,690
I could contact Kayoko Senba's son,

310
00:27:05,690 --> 00:27:11,110
but he said his mother left for a vacation.

311
00:27:11,110 --> 00:27:13,040
I see.

312
00:27:14,080 --> 00:27:15,760
What're you up to?

313
00:27:16,490 --> 00:27:20,010
I figured I'd stop being
a corporate bootlicker.

314
00:27:40,230 --> 00:27:42,400
The police contacted you?

315
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:45,930
No. Don't tell a soul I'm here.

316
00:27:48,210 --> 00:27:51,000
I'll be fine.

317
00:27:51,650 --> 00:27:55,180
You take care as well, alright?

318
00:28:03,490 --> 00:28:09,210
Sir, the elevator is for guests only.

319
00:28:10,340 --> 00:28:13,540
May I ask for your room key?

320
00:28:15,730 --> 00:28:18,560
Has Tomoe contacted you?

321
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:23,790
What is that woman doing?

322
00:28:26,570 --> 00:28:31,450
I hope you've been feeding Keita well.

323
00:28:35,190 --> 00:28:37,060
Room service is here.

324
00:28:37,060 --> 00:28:39,220
I'll stay in touch.

325
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:55,190
I've brought your water.

326
00:28:55,190 --> 00:28:56,980
Would you leave it inside?

327
00:28:56,980 --> 00:29:00,020
Of course.

328
00:29:24,330 --> 00:29:26,940
[Mikio Maehara]

329
00:29:39,460 --> 00:29:42,900
[Tsuyoshi Kojima]
[Xin Ming Ah Japan Representative]

330
00:29:42,900 --> 00:29:46,420
[Dear Haruka Nanase,
I believe we can assist you...]

331
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:15,500
Haruka! Where are you going?

332
00:30:15,500 --> 00:30:19,290
To meet someone. I'll be fine alone.

333
00:30:19,290 --> 00:30:20,920
Wait.

334
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:26,220
"Do all that you can today,
to see further progress tomorrow."

335
00:30:26,910 --> 00:30:30,460
I know that one. Isaac Newton.

336
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:36,010
Not bad.

337
00:30:55,690 --> 00:30:58,060
You really came alone.

338
00:31:02,690 --> 00:31:04,940
I wouldn't disobey the President's son.

339
00:31:04,940 --> 00:31:07,040
Without telling my father?

340
00:31:11,370 --> 00:31:14,280
What did you need to ask me?

341
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:16,210
Or is this about your father?

342
00:31:16,210 --> 00:31:18,640
Tell me where Shiharu is.

343
00:31:20,150 --> 00:31:21,590
Her again.

344
00:31:21,590 --> 00:31:24,580
I have the all the findings from Roopkund.

345
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:28,410
What are you referring to?

346
00:31:29,280 --> 00:31:32,810
The research you people
are so desperate to hide.

347
00:31:36,900 --> 00:31:39,500
Show me, and maybe it'll ring a bell.

348
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:49,810
Creating Shiharu from the bones of Roopkund.
Does that help?

349
00:32:02,350 --> 00:32:04,040
Please.

350
00:32:05,130 --> 00:32:06,970
Tell me where she is.

351
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:10,890
Where is Shiharu?

352
00:32:13,990 --> 00:32:15,800
Create?

353
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:19,580
You say we "created" your sister?

354
00:32:29,160 --> 00:32:31,130
Drop the act, now.

355
00:32:34,030 --> 00:32:37,680
That girl only exists in your mind.

356
00:32:39,780 --> 00:32:41,520
Are you like Kayoko Senba?

357
00:32:43,370 --> 00:32:48,680
Were you also told the cloning was a failure?

358
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:53,650
No, I won't believe that.

359
00:32:54,770 --> 00:32:56,850
Because you people...

360
00:32:57,910 --> 00:33:01,850
You people murdered Professor Ishimizaki
to keep Shiharu a secret!

361
00:33:01,850 --> 00:33:05,250
- What?
- And he's not the only one you've killed!

362
00:33:08,710 --> 00:33:12,750
I see.

363
00:33:12,750 --> 00:33:15,150
I get it now.

364
00:33:15,150 --> 00:33:20,490
Your search has brought
plenty of others misfortune.

365
00:33:20,490 --> 00:33:23,020
Kyoichi Nanase's the one giving orders.

366
00:33:23,020 --> 00:33:27,950
He just wants to keep his company afloat!

367
00:33:30,230 --> 00:33:32,590
I can't be entertaining your delusions.

368
00:33:32,590 --> 00:33:36,000
You're his right-hand man.
I know you know everything!

369
00:33:44,630 --> 00:33:46,680
What?

370
00:33:49,670 --> 00:33:52,250
I don't know anything.

371
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:56,720
Not a damn thing.

372
00:34:17,730 --> 00:34:19,460
Mari.

373
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:27,830
Is this about...

374
00:34:29,540 --> 00:34:34,120
I'm sorry. We haven't made much progress
in regards to your father's case.

375
00:34:34,120 --> 00:34:36,150
I see.

376
00:34:36,150 --> 00:34:39,740
But this case is strange, in many ways.

377
00:34:39,740 --> 00:34:43,000
So I had something I wanted to ask.

378
00:34:43,790 --> 00:34:45,440
Alright.

379
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:49,150
When Nanase was attacked
by the man named Ushio,

380
00:34:49,150 --> 00:34:54,060
he claimed he was accompanied
by Professor Ishimizaki's niece.

381
00:34:54,060 --> 00:34:57,660
But that was you, wasn't it?

382
00:34:59,580 --> 00:35:03,130
Well, I...

383
00:35:03,130 --> 00:35:06,610
I'm not trying to interrogate you about that.

384
00:35:06,610 --> 00:35:08,810
Let me rephrase my question.

385
00:35:08,810 --> 00:35:14,600
You were helping Nanase
search for his sister, correct?

386
00:35:19,310 --> 00:35:25,200
Except, this sister of his
doesn't exist on paper.

387
00:35:30,450 --> 00:35:33,550
I want to start by searching for this person.

388
00:35:35,310 --> 00:35:36,750
What?

389
00:35:39,620 --> 00:35:46,620
This time, I want to try
believing in Haruka Nanase.

390
00:35:48,020 --> 00:35:53,640
Is there anything you know
about Shiharu Nanase?

391
00:36:00,230 --> 00:36:04,520
People who have no citizenship
each have their own reasons.

392
00:36:04,520 --> 00:36:09,040
If Shiharu is in a similar situation,
we must find her right away.

393
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:10,400
As it stands now,

394
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:14,040
she's unable to receive
legal medical attention should she need it.

395
00:36:22,020 --> 00:36:28,210
Shiharu Nanase exists somewhere, doesn't she?

396
00:36:35,120 --> 00:36:38,080
Reach out again when you're ready to talk.

397
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:43,140
I mostly wanted to break the ice today.

398
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:58,650
Haruka. Where are you?

399
00:36:58,650 --> 00:37:01,020
<i>Is Shiharu dead?</i>

400
00:37:02,480 --> 00:37:05,050
You must've heard from Ishimizaki's daughter.

401
00:37:08,460 --> 00:37:11,210
How can you act so nonchalant?

402
00:37:12,540 --> 00:37:14,010
You...

403
00:37:15,560 --> 00:37:18,840
Do you realize what you've done?

404
00:37:19,780 --> 00:37:21,650
Of course.

405
00:37:28,570 --> 00:37:30,660
Did you...

406
00:37:34,390 --> 00:37:36,290
Did you kill Shiharu?

407
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:44,310
<i>You used my mother to create a clone.</i>

408
00:37:44,310 --> 00:37:47,180
Isn't that why she died?

409
00:37:48,450 --> 00:37:50,800
Who told you that?

410
00:37:51,660 --> 00:37:53,500
<i>Kayoko Senba.</i>

411
00:37:54,380 --> 00:37:57,220
I have all the files on Roopkund as well.

412
00:37:58,330 --> 00:38:01,580
What sort of stunts did you pull?

413
00:38:01,580 --> 00:38:04,050
I haven't caused anyone trouble.

414
00:38:05,610 --> 00:38:07,410
At least, not yet.

415
00:38:11,620 --> 00:38:13,130
Haruka.

416
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:16,540
Shiharu is alive.

417
00:38:17,470 --> 00:38:21,620
Shiharu is very much alive.

418
00:38:21,620 --> 00:38:26,840
<i>You must realize the information you have
is a burden to her.</i>

419
00:38:28,350 --> 00:38:30,120
Why?

420
00:38:32,580 --> 00:38:35,750
Why are you doing all this?

421
00:38:36,770 --> 00:38:38,920
Everything I do is for Shiharu's sake.

422
00:38:41,660 --> 00:38:43,800
Where is she?

423
00:38:47,410 --> 00:38:50,160
Where the hell is Shiharu?

424
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:56,410
Let's talk in person. Alone.

425
00:38:57,960 --> 00:38:59,980
Trust me.

426
00:39:00,950 --> 00:39:03,710
<i>You have no other choice.</i>

427
00:39:15,950 --> 00:39:19,210
<i>"No venting allowed, Haruka."</i>

428
00:39:43,520 --> 00:39:46,750
I'm glad you've come.

429
00:39:49,460 --> 00:39:50,910
Follow me.

430
00:39:52,270 --> 00:39:56,520
You've made a sound decision, Haruka Nanase.

431
00:39:56,520 --> 00:39:58,520
You said you'd help, but how?

432
00:39:58,520 --> 00:40:00,960
Please, have a seat.

433
00:40:04,460 --> 00:40:10,850
I hear you suspect your step-father
and head of Nichie Pharmaceutical,

434
00:40:10,850 --> 00:40:16,890
Kyoichi Nanase, of a number of things.

435
00:40:16,890 --> 00:40:19,700
What bothers you most?
The thing with your mother?

436
00:40:19,700 --> 00:40:22,320
Or your missing sister?

437
00:40:22,320 --> 00:40:25,100
I see Hirama has told you of my situation.

438
00:40:26,310 --> 00:40:32,770
I will admit. We have done
our own investigating as well.

439
00:40:32,770 --> 00:40:38,410
As such, I believe our goals
are aligned with one another.

440
00:40:39,060 --> 00:40:40,540
How so?

441
00:40:40,540 --> 00:40:45,380
If Nichie goes under, it becomes easier
for both of us to take action.

442
00:40:48,020 --> 00:40:51,520
Nichie Pharmaceutical -
or rather, Kyoichi Nanase,

443
00:40:51,520 --> 00:40:57,650
who has dabbled in cloning tech,
is now Plantae's loyal dog.

444
00:40:57,650 --> 00:41:00,150
Let me cut to the chase.

445
00:41:06,150 --> 00:41:10,800
Please think of this money
as our way of aiding your search.

446
00:41:12,870 --> 00:41:14,970
What is it you want from me?

447
00:41:18,030 --> 00:41:22,010
You have the data on Roopkund, yes?

448
00:41:24,780 --> 00:41:26,280
I had a feeling.

449
00:41:26,280 --> 00:41:30,600
Our hope is for Nichie
to be officially prosecuted.

450
00:41:30,600 --> 00:41:31,870
Furthermore,

451
00:41:31,870 --> 00:41:36,200
we plan to re-establish the company
as a trustworthy corporation.

452
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:39,900
Though human cloning is illegal,

453
00:41:39,900 --> 00:41:43,720
the technology behind it can be used
for medical advancements.

454
00:41:44,790 --> 00:41:47,430
I was a fool for expecting anything from you.

455
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:56,000
Negotiations haven't ended yet.

456
00:41:58,210 --> 00:42:00,690
Think about it.

457
00:42:00,690 --> 00:42:05,310
The circumstances surrounding Shiharu
grow unruly by the day.

458
00:42:05,310 --> 00:42:09,190
Surely, you cannot protect her alone.

459
00:42:10,100 --> 00:42:14,850
<i>I suspect your younger sister
is the one behind all this.</i>

460
00:42:15,500 --> 00:42:19,660
We will hold onto the data,
for your own safety as well.

461
00:42:32,120 --> 00:42:34,650
A wise choice indeed.

462
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:43,260
Don't ever bother me again.

463
00:42:43,920 --> 00:42:45,590
You're in my way.

464
00:42:45,590 --> 00:42:47,720
Bastard...

465
00:42:48,310 --> 00:42:54,380
If I don't report back to Hirama,
he will call the police on you.

466
00:43:02,940 --> 00:43:05,910
It seems there's been a misunderstanding.

467
00:43:05,910 --> 00:43:08,320
I only wished to talk business with you.

468
00:43:08,320 --> 00:43:10,390
Well, I'm not interested.

469
00:43:11,120 --> 00:43:14,710
Then please, make your way out.

470
00:43:24,200 --> 00:43:25,660
You alright?

471
00:43:25,660 --> 00:43:27,730
Barely.

472
00:43:27,730 --> 00:43:30,880
<i>So? Did you get anything good out of them?</i>

473
00:43:30,880 --> 00:43:32,470
No.

474
00:43:32,470 --> 00:43:34,220
<i>Figures.</i>

475
00:43:36,750 --> 00:43:38,960
Sorry about my accusations yesterday.

476
00:43:39,730 --> 00:43:43,100
So, what's your next move?

477
00:43:44,120 --> 00:43:45,920
The same as it's always been.

478
00:43:47,240 --> 00:43:49,660
Find my sister.

479
00:44:01,270 --> 00:44:04,330
<i>Shii, could you give this a taste?</i>

480
00:44:04,330 --> 00:44:05,870
<i>Sure.</i>

481
00:44:11,200 --> 00:44:13,250
That tastes wrong.

482
00:44:16,550 --> 00:44:18,840
It's good enough.

483
00:44:18,840 --> 00:44:19,910
It's not.

484
00:44:19,910 --> 00:44:25,730
"Do all that you can today,
to see further progress tomorrow."

485
00:44:25,730 --> 00:44:28,150
I know that one.

486
00:44:28,150 --> 00:44:30,350
- Isaac Newton!
- Isaac Newton!

487
00:44:48,060 --> 00:44:49,520
Hello?

488
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:54,710
Please help me find Shiharu Nanase.

489
00:45:00,610 --> 00:45:01,980
Hello?

490
00:45:04,810 --> 00:45:06,860
A package, for me?

491
00:45:47,270 --> 00:45:50,490
[Keita]

492
00:45:51,320 --> 00:45:53,280
[Keita]
